#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0058 expect=skipped domain=VS
#note "CORPUS-WIDE PIN of the GET_MODEL_COLUMN_ORDER empty-resolution skip: with no '#library model-column-order' declared for VS, OperationExecutor maps the null/empty getStandardModelVariables result to LIBRARY_NOT_AVAILABLE and RuleRunner reports the rule SKIPPED for the dataset. Same VS dataset as the invalid body (incl. VSCUSTOM) so the fixture is discriminating: with an order declared it would fire."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VSTEST   type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Name"
col VSORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col VSCUSTOM type=Char label="Sponsor Defined Variable"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | SYSBP | Systolic Blood Pressure | 120 | X
---
